course: dictionary
lesson: 2985
title: A duet is two together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A duet is a piece of music for two singers or two players, or a performance by two people together. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Gibbons are small apes that sing loud duets, male and female together, heard about a kilometre away.» The words male and female together tell you that a duet has two voices.
explain: A duet can also be a call, not only a song. «Pairs of red-crowned cranes dance and call in duets» means two birds calling together, one call answering the other. The clue is pairs: two cranes, two parts.
explain: Look at the words that sit beside it. Solo means one, trio means three and quartet means four. A duet must be two, because duet fits between them in the same family of words. Try your meaning in the sentence: if "two together" still makes sense, you have it.
fact: A duet is for two: two singers, two players, or two people performing together.
fact: «Duet» is a noun: a duet, duets.
fact: Solo means one, trio means three and quartet means four.
fact: «Duet» can also be a rare verb: to duet means to perform a duet, as in «duetted» and «duetting».
fact: «Gibbons are small apes that sing loud duets, male and female together, heard about a kilometre away.»
exercise: «Gibbons are small apes that sing loud duets, male and female together.» What is a duet here? | A quiet whisper | A small ape | *Two voices singing together | A song for one voice
exercise: A trio has three people and a quartet has four. What is a solo? | *One person alone | Four people together | Three people together | Two people together
exercise: «Pairs of red-crowned cranes dance and call in duets.» Who is making the duet in this sentence? | The dancers at a concert | *Pairs of cranes, calling together | Gibbons in the trees | A single crane alone
test: Which word means two people performing together? | *Duet | Solo | Trio | Quartet
test: Ella says a duet is always a song for one singer. What is the best answer? | Yes, and it always has four singers | Yes, a duet is always a solo | No, a duet is a kind of ape | *No, a duet can be a performance by two people together, and two birds can make one too
exam: Use the clues in «Gibbons are small apes that sing loud duets, male and female together, heard about a kilometre away.» What can you say about a duet? | It is a dance with no sound | It is always quiet | Only one gibbon sings it | *It is sung by two, and it can be heard a long way off
